This project is an Ilium plugin. Follow AGENTS.md at the repository root; the essentials are repeated here.

- Docs: fetch http://127.0.0.1:4327/llms.txt, then the page you need as Markdown. Do not invent APIs, manifest keys or capability names.
- Commands: `ilium plugin new`, `build`, `check`, `dev`, `pack`. TypeScript uses Bun only.
- Events in, intents out. Handler: Rust `fn on_events(&mut self, batch: Vec<Event>) -> Vec<Submission>`; TypeScript `onEvents(batch: Event[]): Submission[]`.
- Declare capabilities and every contribution in `manifest.json`. Ask for the smallest grant.
- Never block: `on-events` has a 20 ms deadline. Slow work is a request or a background job.
- Retained mode: set decorations, virtual rows and toolbar state once; views return from `render`.
- Test with the fake host (`FakeHost` in Rust, `createFakeHost()` in TypeScript).
- Every example and answer covers both Rust and TypeScript unless the project uses one.
